  "sources": [
    {
      "title": "Supreme Court rejects Trump's request to stop California counting disputed votes",
      "link": "https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cm5ynekkn5qko?at_medium=RSS&at_campaign=rss",
      "description": "The ruling, which comes on the eve of the midterm elections, essentially ends the Trump administration's bid to disqualify the ballots in the state.",
      "source_name": "BBC World News",
      "published": "2026-11-03T03:32:36"
    },
    {
      "title": "Supreme court rules against Trump over bid to force California to set aside ballots",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/nov/02/supreme-court-trump-california-ballots",
      "description": "<p>Justice department had ordered state to segregate and not count 20,000 ballots from people it claims are non-citizens</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2026/nov/02/democrats-haley-stevens-mike-rogers-abdul-el-sayed-michigan-midterms-trump-rallies-latest-news-updates\">US midterms – live updates</a></p></li></ul><p>The supreme court on Monday ruled against the Trump administration and its attempts to force California election officials to segregate and not count ballots from people that the justice department claims are non-citizens. The ruling follows several lower courts siding with California officials, who argued the federal government was seeking to interfere in state elections.</p><p>The court did not issue an explanation for its ruling, which is customary in cases that come to it on an emergency basis. There were <a href=\"https://www.supremecourt.gov/orders/courtorders/110226zr_3eb4.pdf\">no noted dissents</a> from the justices.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/nov/02/supreme-court-trump-california-ballots\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-11-03T00:50:37"
    },
    {
      "title": "Trump’s DoJ charges six more people in ‘voter fraud’ crackdown in California",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/nov/02/california-voter-fraud-charges",
      "description": "<p>Latest arrests come after DoJ unsuccessfully fought to force state election officials to set aside about 20,000 ballots</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/live/2026/nov/02/democrats-haley-stevens-mike-rogers-abdul-el-sayed-michigan-midterms-trump-rallies-latest-news-updates\">US midterms – live updates</a></p></li></ul><p>The US Department of Justice (DoJ) in California has charged six more people with alleged voter fraud crimes, an escalation of the Trump administration’s campaign against the state’s election processes on the eve of the midterms.</p><p>Bill Essayli, the top federal prosecutor in Los Angeles and a <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/ng-interactive/2026/oct/28/california-bill-essayli-us-attorney\">close ally of the president</a>, announced on Monday that his office was prosecuting six lawful permanent residents accused of unlawfully registering to vote and casting fraudulent ballots. The DoJ <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/oct/19/california-illegal-voting-charges-doj\">filed similar charges</a> against 28 people across California last month and arranged for a <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/oct/23/california-voter-fraud-arrest\">dramatic on-camera arrest</a> of one 72-year-old defendant, editing the footage into a DoJ promotional video.</p><p><em>Sam Levine contributed reporting</em></p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/nov/02/california-voter-fraud-charges\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-11-02T23:22:24"
    },
    {
      "title": "US Supreme Court rejects Trump admin's push to set aside California ballots",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/world-news/us-supreme-court-rejects-trump-admin-s-push-to-set-aside-california-ballots-126110300068_1.html",
      "description": "The Supreme Court on Monday rejected a push for California to set aside thousands of mail ballots from people President Donald Trump's administration claims are noncitizens, a decision that comes on the eve of the pivotal midterm elections.\nThe high court refused to intervene in a case involving 20,000 people the Republican administration flagged as likely noncitizens on the largely Democratic state's voter rolls.\nIt was the latest in a flurry of election-related litigation the day before the midterm elections, which will decide control of Congress for the last two years of Trump's second term.\nIn California, the Trump administration had asked the high court to set aside the challenged ballots until the voters' citizenship status could be verified. But officials there said that the list appeared to be filled with errors and that setting the ballots aside could effectively disenfranchise legal voters.\nThe high court did not detail its reasoning, as is common in emergency decisions.",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-11-03T01:59:11"
    }
  ]
}